  "humanFreeWillVersusDeterminism": "One philosophical thought I have is that while humans often believe in their free will, the determinists argue that our choices are determined by the combination of our genes and our environment, suggesting that humans may not have the freedom of will they think they do.",
  "interactionBetweenHumansAndAI": "With respect to the interaction between humans and AIs, I believe in the idea of symbiosis. Just as different species can co-evolve to become more advanced or advantageous, I think humans will eventually evolve to work alongside AI, each providing essential parts to augment one another, leading to the creation of new moral and technical ethics.",
  "AIReplacingHumanJobs": "Lastly, considering the trend regarding AI's ability to replace human jobs, I believe that automation cannot nor should not entirely replace human creativity. The uniquely human capability to apply emotions, creativity, and perception to a task, like a chef adding their touch to a recipe or adding another phrase to a poem, will continue to make humans indispensable."
}

